        "evidence": "The out-of-scope section states what the theorem does not assert, which is scope, not emphasis-narration.",
        "notes": "SS4d NOTE: but this requires further development and is not committed in this revision is author-tracking status prose and belongs in authorNotes (kind: status). RIGOR: THE ALGEBRA IS CORRECT AND I CHECKED IT. hbar_q^2 h_q [2]_q = ((q-1)^2/q^2)(q-q^{-1})(q+q^{-1}) = (q-1)^2(q^4-1)/q^4, and (q-1)^2(1-q^{-4})/3 = (q-1)^2(q^4-1)/(3q^4), so the ratio is exactly 1/3 as claimed and the strict inequality follows for q > 1. The Skein adjustment (q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})/(q+q^{-1}) = 0.99594 < 1 at q_0, as stated. The Tightness claim also verifies numerically: (1/3)(q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})/(q+q^{-1}) = 0.3319783, and the realised splitting 1.286429856 MeV over the bound 3.875042037 MeV is 0.3319783 - agreement to 7 figures. CAVEAT: that half-power adjustment factor is 1/z_C/(q+q^{-1}), i.e. it inherits the convention-C leak recorded on prop:flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split; under the canonical convention D the realised-splitting fraction changes. TWO MINOR DEFECTS: (a) four cross-references are written as relative .md paths (flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split.md, ../observations/flavor-split-substrate.md, hecke-convergence-bound.md, ../observations/dressed-quark-numerology-at-q0.md) rather than the chapter's #label anchors, so they will not resolve as hyperrefs; (b) the slack-ratio display ends in a comma and the next sentence begins capitalised."
